 # Changelog
 
+## [2.4.0] - 2026-10-16
+
+### Model Testing Studio
+
+A new **Testing** panel turns the app into a benchmarking platform: run
+several GGUF models back-to-back on CPU, watch their real speed, and record
+the screen to share.
+
+### Added
+- **Model Testing Studio** (`ggufloader/core/testing/`) - loads each selected
+  GGUF in turn, runs a fixed prompt workload through it, measures real
+  time-to-first-token and decode tokens/sec from llama.cpp's own stream,
+  unloads it, then moves to the next model.
+- **Live leaderboard** - the Testing panel ranks models by tokens/sec as they
+  finish, with TTFT, load time, and per-prompt detail.
+- **Screen recording** - capture the app window to a `.webm` with the browser's
+  MediaRecorder, with a live stats HUD rendered inside the window so the speed
+  is visible in the video; packaged Electron builds save straight to disk
+  through a new `save-recording` IPC bridge.
+- **Shareable reports** - export any run as JSON, Markdown, or CSV.
+- **REST routes** under `/api/benchmark/suite/*`, plus `/api/benchmark/run`
+  (the frontend client already called this endpoint, but the backend never
+  implemented it).
+
+### Notes
+- Benchmarks run on **CPU by default**; a GPU toggle is available.
+- The pinned chat model is left untouched: the studio frees the global backend
+  before a run and re-triggers the startup auto-loader afterwards, so the
+  "at most one Llama" invariant holds.
+- Sample choice and docs: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-model-testing-studio-design.md`.
+
