+# Model Testing Studio — design
+
+**Date:** 2026-10-16
+**Status:** implemented
+
+## Goal
+
+Turn GGUF Loader into a testing platform that runs **several GGUF models
+back-to-back on CPU**, measures their real speed (time-to-first-token and
+decode tokens/sec), shows a live leaderboard, and lets the user **record the
+screen** so the speed differences can be shown to other people.
+
+## Why this needs new code
+
+- The app is deliberately pinned to one model. `api/routes/model.py`'s
+  `_require_pinned_target` gate rejects every other GGUF, so "run different
+  models" is blocked at the HTTP layer.
+- `core/agent/benchmark.py` already has a `ModelBenchmark` engine that
+  measures tok/s + TTFT from a plain callable, and the UI can list past
+  reports — but there is **no way to actually start a run** from the UI, and
+  it measures a single already-loaded model (it never swaps models).
+- The frontend `benchmarkApi.run` client call targets `/api/benchmark/run`,
+  which does not exist on the backend.
+
+## Architecture
+
+```
+frontend/src/components/agent/TestingStudioPanel.tsx
+  |  REST (poll)                        getDisplayMedia + MediaRecorder
+  v                                              v
+/api/benchmark/suite/*  ---------------->  .webm recording (browser); saved to
+  |                                          disk via Electron IPC when packaged
+  v
+ggufloader/core/testing/runner.py  (SuiteRunner)
+  |  load_fn / unload_fn  (injected; default = core/router.py + ModelBackend)
+  v
+one llama.cpp model at a time (CPU by default)
+```
+
+### Key decisions
+
+1. **Separate benchmark path, pinned chat model untouched.** The suite runner
+   never calls the pinned-target gate. The API layer frees the app's global
+   backend before a run and re-triggers the startup auto-loader afterwards, so
+   the "at most one `Llama`" invariant holds.
+2. **Real metrics, measured from the stream.** TTFT = wall time from request
+   to the first streamed piece; tokens/sec = tokenizer token count of the
+   generated text divided by decode wall time (`first piece -> last piece`).
+   Sampling is greedy (temperature 0, top_k 1) so runs are comparable.
+3. **Fixed workload.** A small, fixed prompt set (`SUITE_PROMPTS`) with a
+   per-prompt `max_tokens` cap, so every model does the same work.
+4. **Injected I/O for testability.** `SuiteRunner` takes `load_fn` /
+   `unload_fn` / `clock`, so the whole engine is headless-testable with a
+   fake backend (no model, no GPU). This matches the repo's "tests are
+   headless" convention.
+5. **Polling, not WebSocket.** Benchmark state is polled (~700 ms) from
+   `/api/benchmark/suite/status`. It is simpler and does not touch the
+   WebSocket event contract.
+6. **Recording = capture the window.** `getDisplayMedia` + `MediaRecorder`
+   record the app window to `.webm`. A recording HUD overlay shows the live
+   tok/s while recording, so the video itself displays the speed.
+
+## Backend surface
+
+`ggufloader/core/testing/runner.py`
+
+- `SuitePrompt`, `PromptResult`, `ModelResult`, `SuiteRun` dataclasses
+- `SUITE_PROMPTS` — the fixed workload
+- `SuiteRunner.run(paths, device, prompt_ids, max_tokens, n_ctx, on_event)`
+- `SuiteRunner.cancel()`
+- `SuiteStore` — save / get / list runs as JSON
+- `export_markdown(run)` / `export_csv(run)`
+
+`ggufloader/api/routes/benchmark.py` (added to the existing router)
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| GET | `/api/benchmark/suite/prompts` | the fixed workload |
+| GET | `/api/benchmark/suite/models` | candidate GGUFs (reuses the model catalog) |
+| POST | `/api/benchmark/suite/run` | start a run (background thread) |
+| GET | `/api/benchmark/suite/status` | live progress + partial results |
+| POST | `/api/benchmark/suite/cancel` | cooperative cancel |
+| GET | `/api/benchmark/suite/runs` | saved runs |
+| GET | `/api/benchmark/suite/runs/{id}` | one run |
+| GET | `/api/benchmark/suite/runs/{id}/export` | `json` \| `markdown` \| `csv` |
+| POST | `/api/benchmark/run` | single-model convenience run (starts a 1-model suite) |
+
+## Frontend surface
+
+- `frontend/src/hooks/useScreenRecorder.ts` — `getDisplayMedia` capture to a
+  downloadable `.webm` (with an Electron save-to-disk path).
+- `frontend/src/components/agent/TestingStudioPanel.tsx` — model picker, run
+  controls, live progress, leaderboard bars, recording controls, export.
+- Registered as a sidebar plugin (`id: 'testing'`) and wired in `RightPanel`.
+- `electron/main.ts` + `preload.ts` — `save-recording` IPC so packaged builds
+  can write the video straight to disk.
+
+## Testing
+
+- `tests/unit/test_testing_studio.py` — headless: measurement math, ordering,
+  error isolation, cancellation, store round-trip, exports, route presence.
+- `python -m pytest tests/unit` — full suite stays green.
+- `cd frontend && npx tsc --noEmit && npm run build`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- GPU benchmarking parity (device flag exists; default is CPU as requested).
+- Real-time video compositing of charts into the recording (the HUD overlay is
+  what gets captured).
+- Downloading models from the studio (the model chip already does that; the
+  studio only lists GGUFs already on disk).
